   "id": "summary_ferry",
   "max_tokens": 1024,
   "messages": [
    {
     "content": "Summarize the following in at most 40 words.\n\nThe Sundial Island ferry operator said on Wednesday that it will switch to a winter timetable from 12 October. Crossings between Port Marlow and the island will drop from eight a day to five, with the first boat leaving at 7:10 am and the last at 5:40 pm. Fares remain unchanged at 9 for adults and 4 for children, but the operator is ending its cash payment option and will accept only cards and the Sundial travel pass. The change follows a fall in passenger numbers of almost a third since August and the planned refit of the larger vessel, the Aurelia, which will be out of service until March. A smaller boat, the Wren, will cover the route and cannot carry more than six cars, so vehicle bookings must be made at least two days ahead. Island residents who depend on the early crossing for work were invited to a meeting at the community hall on 2 October, where the operator's manager, Beatriz Calloway, will take questions. Freight deliveries will continue on Tuesdays and Fridays, and a water taxi can be arranged for emergencies by calling the harbour office.",
     "role": "user"
    }
   ],
   "source": "authored",
   "tool_set": null
  },
  {
   "expect": {
    "contains_all": [
